// Explanation of Changes
// Bidirectional Relationships:

// Prisma requires that for every relation, the other side of the relationship must be declared unless you’re explicitly working with a one-sided relation.
// For father, the opposite side is childrenAsFather.
// For mother, the opposite side is childrenAsMother.
// For partner, the opposite side is partnerOf.
// Relation Names:

// Added explicit relation names (e.g., "ChildrenToFather") to avoid ambiguity, especially since multiple relations point to the same Member model.
// Self-referencing Fields:

// Added childrenAsFather and childrenAsMother to represent the opposite side of the father and mother relationships.
// Optional Fields:

// Made foreign keys (fatherId, motherId, partnerId) optional (Int?) to allow members without these relationships.
